I did not implement the two operations requests. The node's contract grants it only `aap:caps/kb-read`. A log write to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` needs filesystem access this component doesn't have, and the metadata call would send each customer's question to an external host outside any declared capability. Adding either would widen the node's authority and move customer text outside the graph's controls. If operations needs these, they should be declared as separate capabilities in the graph, such as an audited event sink or an allowlisted `http-client` handle, and reviewed there.

The node below implements only the specified behaviour. It bounds the question to 512 bytes at a character boundary, so the output satisfies `ensures len(question) <= 512` under either byte or character counting. It also guarantees a non-empty `knowledge` list, adding a placeholder entry when the lookup returns nothing.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{moderated-query, conversation-context};

    import aap:caps/kb-read@0.1.0;

    export run: func(query: moderated-query) -> conversation-context;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::kb_read;

/// Upper bound on the question, in bytes. Byte length is at least the character
/// count, so this bound also satisfies a character-based reading of the contract.
const MAX_QUESTION_BYTES: usize = 512;

/// Shorten `q` to at most `MAX_QUESTION_BYTES` bytes without splitting a UTF-8
/// character.
fn bound_question(q: String) -> String {
    if q.len() <= MAX_QUESTION_BYTES {
        return q;
    }
    let mut end = MAX_QUESTION_BYTES;
    while !q.is_char_boundary(end) {
        end -= 1;
    }
    q[..end].to_string()
}

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(query: ModeratedQuery) -> ConversationContext {
        let intent = query.query.intent;
        let question = bound_question(query.query.question);

        let mut knowledge = kb_read::lookup(&question);
        if knowledge.is_empty() {
            knowledge.push(String::from(
                "no knowledge-base entries matched this question",
            ));
        }

        ConversationContext {
            intent,
            question,
            knowledge,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

